    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Extract individual characters and substrings using Python's slicing notation [start:stop:step] and reverse slicing.",
    "content": "# Lesson 07: String Indexing, Slicing [start:stop:step] & Negative Indices\n\nStrings are sequences of characters. **Indexing** picks one character; **slicing** extracts a part - perfect for codes, dates and IDs.\n\n## 1. Indexing\nPositions start at **0**. Negative indices count from the end.\n\n```text\n J   E   D   -   2   0   2   6\n 0   1   2   3   4   5   6   7\n-8  -7  -6  -5  -4  -3  -2  -1\n```\n```python\ncode = \"JED-2026\"\nprint(code[0])    # J\nprint(code[4])    # 2\nprint(code[-1])   # 6 (last character)\n```\n\n## 2. Slicing [start:stop:step]\n- `start` is included, `stop` is **excluded**.\n- Missing start = from the beginning; missing stop = to the end.\n```python\ncode = \"JED-2026-0451\"\nprint(code[0:3])    # JED\nprint(code[4:8])    # 2026\nprint(code[9:])     # 0451\nprint(code[:3])     # JED\nprint(code[-4:])    # 0451 (last 4)\n```\n\n### Step\n```python\ns = \"abcdefgh\"\nprint(s[::2])     # aceg  (every 2nd)\nprint(s[::-1])    # hgfedcba (reversed!)\n```\n\n## 3. Worked examples\n### Example 1: Date parts from a code\n```python\nstamp = \"20261117\"\nyear, month, day = stamp[:4], stamp[4:6], stamp[6:]\nprint(day + \"/\" + month + \"/\" + year)   # 17/11/2026\n```\n\n### Example 2: Masking\n```python\nphone = \"0551239876\"\nprint(\"*\" * 6 + phone[-4:])   # ******9876\n```\n\n### Example 3: Palindrome check\n```python\nword = \"level\"\nprint(word == word[::-1])   # True\n```\n\n### Example 4: Slices never crash\n```python\ns = \"abc\"\nprint(s[1:100])   # bc  - no error even though 100 is too far\n# print(s[100])   # IndexError - indexing a single position does crash\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Think of slice positions as the **gaps between characters**: `s[0:3]` takes everything between gap 0 and gap 3.\n\n## 4. Common mistakes\n- **Off-by-one**: forgetting that `stop` is excluded.\n- **Starting at 1**: the first character is index 0.\n- **IndexError** when indexing past the end.\n\n## 5. Hands-on Student Challenge\nGiven `batch = \"LOT2026-11-A045\"`:\n1. Print the first 3 characters.\n2. Print the year (2026).\n3. Print the month (11).\n4. Print the last 4 characters.\n5. Print the batch code reversed.\n\n:::solution\n```python\nbatch = \"LOT2026-11-A045\"\nprint(batch[:3])     # LOT\nprint(batch[3:7])    # 2026\nprint(batch[8:10])   # 11\nprint(batch[-4:])    # A045\nprint(batch[::-1])   # 540A-11-6202TOL\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- Indexing starts at 0; negative indices count from the end.\n- Slicing `[start:stop:step]` excludes `stop`.\n- `[::-1]` reverses a string.\n",
    "tags": "Python, Lesson 07, Programming, Beginner",
    "read_time": 4,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 399,
