    "id": "py-74",
    "lesson_number": 74,
    "title": "Lesson 74: Regular Expressions Basics: re.search() and re.findall()",
    "slug": "python-lesson-74-regular-expressions-basics-re-search-and-re-findall",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "python",
    "track_name": "Python Path",
    "category_name": "Python Programming",
    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Match complex text patterns, email addresses, and phone numbers using Python's re module.",
    "content": "# Lesson 74: Regular Expressions Basics: re.search() and re.findall()\n\n**Regular expressions** (regex) describe text **patterns**: \"10 digits starting with 05\", \"an email address\", \"INV- followed by numbers\". The `re` module searches text for them.\n\n## 1. Core functions\n- `re.search(pattern, text)` - first match anywhere (or None).\n- `re.findall(pattern, text)` - list of **all** matches.\n- `re.fullmatch(pattern, text)` - does the **whole** text match?\n- Write patterns as raw strings: `r\"\\d+\"`.\n\n## 2. Pattern building blocks\n\n| Pattern | Matches |\n|---|---|\n| `\\d` | A digit 0-9 |\n| `\\w` | A letter, digit or underscore |\n| `\\s` | Whitespace |\n| `.` | Any character |\n| `[abc]` / `[A-Z]` | One of these / a range |\n| `+` | One or more |\n| `*` | Zero or more |\n| `?` | Optional |\n| `{3}` / `{2,4}` | Exactly 3 / 2 to 4 times |\n| `^` / `$` | Start / end of text |\n| `( )` | A group (captured part) |\n\n## 3. Worked examples\n### Example 1: Find all numbers\n```python\nimport re\ntext = \"Order 4521: 12 boxes of Gel at 40 SAR, 5 boxes of Drops at 32 SAR\"\nprint(re.findall(r\"\\d+\", text))    # ['4521', '12', '40', '5', '32']\n```\n\n### Example 2: Validate a Saudi mobile number\n```python\nimport re\nfor phone in [\"0501234567\", \"0551234\", \"+966501234567\", \"0601234567\"]:\n    ok = re.fullmatch(r\"05\\d{8}\", phone)\n    print(phone, bool(ok))\n```\n\n### Example 3: Find invoice numbers\n```python\nimport re\ntext = \"Paid INV-1045 and INV-1102, pending INV-0987.\"\nprint(re.findall(r\"INV-\\d{4}\", text))   # ['INV-1045', 'INV-1102', 'INV-0987']\n```\n\n### Example 4: Groups - extract parts\n```python\nimport re\nm = re.search(r\"(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})\", \"Report date: 2026-11-17\")\nif m:\n    year, month, day = m.groups()\n    print(day, month, year)        # 17 11 2026\n    print(m.group(0))              # the full match: 2026-11-17\n```\n\n### Example 5: Emails (simple pattern)\n```python\nimport re\ntext = \"Contact sara@company.com or info@nahdi.sa for details.\"\nprint(re.findall(r\"[\\w.+-]+@[\\w-]+\\.[\\w.]+\", text))\n```\n\n### Example 6: Case-insensitive search\n```python\nimport re\nprint(bool(re.search(r\"gel\", \"Eye GEL 10ml\", re.IGNORECASE)))   # True\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Test patterns on **regex101.com** (choose the Python flavour) - it explains every part of the pattern and highlights matches live.\n\n## 4. Common mistakes\n- **Forgetting the `r` prefix** - `\"\\d\"` may be misread; use `r\"\\d\"`.\n- **`search` vs `fullmatch`** - `search` finds a match *inside* longer text.\n- **Overly complex patterns** for simple jobs that `in` or `split` can do.\n\n## 5. Hands-on Student Challenge\n```python\nlog = \"\"\"2026-11-15 ERROR order INV-1045 failed for user ahmed@company.com\n2026-11-16 INFO order INV-1102 ok\n2026-11-17 ERROR order INV-0987 failed for user sara@company.com\"\"\"\n```\n1. Find all invoice numbers.\n2. Find all dates.\n3. Find the emails on ERROR lines only.\n4. Count how many lines are errors.\n\n:::solution\n```python\nimport re\n\nlog = \"\"\"2026-11-15 ERROR order INV-1045 failed for user ahmed@company.com\n2026-11-16 INFO order INV-1102 ok\n2026-11-17 ERROR order INV-0987 failed for user sara@company.com\"\"\"\n\nprint(re.findall(r\"INV-\\d{4}\", log))          # ['INV-1045', 'INV-1102', 'INV-0987']\nprint(re.findall(r\"\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\", log))  # ['2026-11-15', '2026-11-16', '2026-11-17']\n\nerror_emails = [re.search(r\"[\\w.+-]+@[\\w-]+\\.\\w+\", line).group()\n                for line in log.splitlines() if \" ERROR \" in line]\nprint(error_emails)                           # ['ahmed@company.com', 'sara@company.com']\n\nprint(len(re.findall(r\"^\\S+ ERROR\", log, re.MULTILINE)))   # 2\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- `re.search`, `re.findall`, `re.fullmatch` find patterns.\n- Learn `\\d \\w \\s . + * ? {n} [ ] ^ $ ( )`.\n- Use raw strings and test patterns on regex101.\n",
    "tags": "Python, Lesson 74, Programming, Advanced",
    "read_time": 4,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
